  {"Magical Pokemon", 9, 44, "Its cry sounds like an incantation. It is said the cry may rarely be imbued with happiness-giving power."},
  {"Big Boss Pokemon", 9, 273, "If one utters a deep cry, many MURKROW gather quickly. For this, it is called \"Summoner of Night.\""},
  {"Catty Pokemon", 5, 39, "It hides its spiteful tendency of hooking its claws into the nose of its Trainer if it isn't fed."},
  {"Tiger Cat Pokemon", 10, 438, "It binds its body with its tails to make itself look bigger. If it locks eyes, it will glare ceaselessly."},
  {"Bell Pokemon", 2, 6, "There is an orb inside its mouth. When it hops, the orb bounces all over and makes a ringing sound."},
  {"Skunk Pokemon", 4, 192, "It sprays a foul fluid from its rear. Its stench spreads over a mile radius, driving Pokemon away."},
  {"Skunk Pokemon", 10, 380, "It attacks by spraying a horribly smelly fluid from the tip of its tail. Attacks from above confound it."},
  {"Bronze Pokemon", 5, 605, "There are researchers who believe this Pokemon reflected like a mirror in the distant past."},
  {"Bronze Bell Pokemon", 13, 1870, "It brought rains by opening portals to another world. It was revered as a bringer of plentiful harvests."},
  {"Bonsai Pokemon", 5, 150, "It prefers an arid atmosphere. It leaks water that looks like tears when adjusting its moisture level."},
  {"Mime Pokemon", 6, 130, "It mimics the expressions and motions of those it sees to understand the feelings of others."},
  {"Playhouse Pokemon", 6, 244, "It likes to carry around a small rock. It may wander around others' feet and cause them to stumble."},
  {"Music Note Pokemon", 5, 19, "Its tongue is just like a human's. As a result, it can cleverly mimic human speech."},
  {"Forbidden Pokemon", 10, 1080, "Its constant mischief and misdeeds resulted in it being bound to an Odd Keystone by a mysterious spell."},
  {"Land Shark Pokemon", 7, 205, "It attacks using its huge mouth. While its attacks are powerful, it hurts itself out of clumsiness, too."},
  {"Cave Pokemon", 14, 560, "It loves sparkly things. It seeks treasures in caves and hoards the loot in its nest."},
  {"Mach Pokemon", 19, 950, "It is said that when one runs at high speed, its wings create blades of wind that can fell nearby trees."},
  {"Big Eater Pokemon", 6, 1050, "In its desperation to gulp down food, it forgets about the food it has hidden under its fur."},
  {"Emanation Pokemon", 7, 202, "It has the peculiar power of being able to see emotions such as joy and rage in the form of waves."},
  {"Aura Pokemon", 12, 540, "A well-trained one can sense auras to identify and take in the feelings of creatures over half a mile away."},
  {"Hippo Pokemon", 8, 495, "It shuts its nostrils tight then travels through sand as if walking. They form colonies of around ten."},
  {"Heavyweight Pokemon", 20, 3000, "It is surprisingly quick to anger. It holds its mouth agape as a display of its strength."},
  {"Scorpion Pokemon", 8, 120, "As soon as the tail claws close, its needle tips secrete poison. It can survive a year without food."},
  {"Ogre Scorp Pokemon", 13, 615, "Possessing a sturdy build, it takes pride in its strength, taking down foes without using toxins."},
  {"Toxic Mouth Pokemon", 7, 230, "It rarely fights fairly, but that is strictly to ensure survival. It is popular as a mascot."},
  {"Toxic Mouth Pokemon", 13, 444, "It has a poison sac at its throat. When it croaks, the stored poison is churned for greater potency."},
  {"Bug Catcher Pokemon", 14, 270, "It binds itself to trees in marshes. It attracts prey with its sweet- smelling drool and gulps them down."},
  {"Wing Fish Pokemon", 4, 70, "The line running down its side can store sunlight. It shines vividly at night."},
  {"Neon Pokemon", 12, 240, "It crawls along the seafloor using its long front fins like legs. It competes for food with LANTURN."},
  {"Kite Pokemon", 10, 650, "People organize tours to see this Pokemon frolic and skim the tops of waves with REMORAID."},
  {"Frost Tree Pokemon", 10, 505, "Seemingly curious about people, they gather around footsteps they find on snowy mountains."},
  {"Frost Tree Pokemon", 22, 1355, "They appear when the snow flowers bloom. When the petals fall, they retreat to places unknown again."},
  {"Sharp Claw Pokemon", 11, 340, "Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders."},
  {"Magnet Area Pokemon", 12, 1800, "A group tried to use scientific means to make MAGNEZONE evolve, but their efforts ended in failure."},
  {"Licking Pokemon", 17, 1400, "The long tongue is always soggy with slobber. The saliva contains a solvent that causes numbness."},
  {"Drill Pokemon", 24, 2828, "It can launch a rock held in its hand like a missile by tightening then expanding muscles instantly."},
  {"Vine Pokemon", 20, 1286, "Its arms are made of plants that bind themselves to things. They grow back right away if cut."},
  {"Thunderbolt Pokemon", 18, 1386, "Heedless of enemy attacks, it closes in, shoves its tails onto the foe, then looses high voltage."},
  {"Blast Pokemon", 16, 680, "When launching 3,600 degrees F fireballs, its body takes on a whitish hue from the intense heat."},
  {"Jubilee Pokemon", 15, 380, "It shares many blessings with people who respect one another's rights and avoid needless strife."},
  {"Ogre Darner Pokemon", 19, 515, "Its jaw power is incredible. It is adept at biting apart foes while flying by at high speed."},
  {"Verdant Pokemon", 10, 255, "It basically does not fight. With cells similar to those of plants, it can perform photosynthesis."},
  {"Fresh Snow Pokemon", 8, 259, "By controlling its body heat, it can freeze the atmosphere around it to make a diamond-dust flurry."},
  {"Fang Scorp Pokemon", 20, 425, "If it succeeds in catching even a faint breeze properly, it can circle the globe without flapping once."},
  {"Twin Tusk Pokemon", 25, 2910, "A frozen one was dug up from soil dating back 10,000 years. It woke up to much amazement."},
  {"Virtual Pokemon", 9, 340, "Its programming was modified to enable work in alien dimensions. It did not work as planned."},
  {"Blade Pokemon", 16, 520, "When trying to protect someone, it extends its elbows as if they were swords and fights savagely."},
  {"Compass Pokemon", 14, 3400, "It freely controls three small units called Mini-Noses using magnetic force."},
  {"Gripper Pokemon", 22, 1066, "It is said to take lost spirits into its pliant body and guide them home."},
  {"Snow Land Pokemon", 13, 266, "It freezes prey by blowing its -58 degrees F breath. It is said to then secretly display its prey."},
  {"Plasma Pokemon", 3, 3, "Its electric-like body can enter some kinds of machines and take control in order to make mischief."},
  {"Knowledge Pokemon", 3, 3, "When UXIE flew, people gained the ability to solve problems. It was the birth of knowledge."},
  {"Emotion Pokemon", 3, 3, "When MESPRIT flew, people learned the joy and sadness of living. It was the birth of emotions."},
  {"Willpower Pokemon", 3, 3, "When AZELF flew, people gained the determination to do things. It was the birth of willpower."},
  {"Temporal Pokemon", 54, 6830, "A legendary Pokemon of Sinnoh. It is said that time flows when DIALGA's heart beats."},
  {"Spatial Pokemon", 42, 3360, "A legendary Pokemon of Sinnoh. It is said that space becomes more stable with PALKIA's every breath."},
  {"Lava Dome Pokemon", 17, 4300, "Its body is made of rugged steel. However, it is partially melted in spots because of its own heat."},
  {"Colossal Pokemon", 37, 4200, "It is said to have made Pokemon that look like itself from a special ice mountain, rocks, and magma."},
  {"Renegade Pokemon", 45, 7500, "It was banished for its violence. It silently gazed upon the old world from the Distortion World."},
  {"Lunar Pokemon", 15, 856, "On nights around the quarter moon, the aurora from its tail extends and undulates beautifully."},
  {"Sea Drifter Pokemon", 4, 31, "It drifts in warm seas. It always returns to where it was born, no matter how far it may have drifted."},
  {"Seafaring Pokemon", 3, 14, "It is born with a wondrous power that lets it bond with any kind of Pokemon."},
  {"Pitch-Black Pokemon", 15, 505, "To protect itself, it afflicts those around it with nightmares. However, it means no harm."},
  {"Gratitude Pokemon", 2, 21, "The flowers all over its body burst into bloom if it is lovingly hugged and senses gratitude."},
  {"Alpha Pokemon", 32, 3200, "It is said to have emerged from an egg in a place where there was nothing, then shaped the world."},
  {"Victory", 4, 40, "This Pokemon brings victory. It is said that Trainers with Victini always win, regardless of the type of encounter."},
  {"Grass Snake", 6, 81, "It is very intelligent and calm. Being exposed to lots of sunlight makes its movements swifter. When they are not feeling well, their tails droop."},
  {"Grass Snake", 8, 160, "When it gets dirty, its leaves can't be used in photosynthesis, so it always keeps clean. They avoid attacks by sinking into the shadows of thick foliage."},
  {"Regal", 33, 630, "They raise their heads to intimidate foes, but only give it their all when fighting powerful opponents who are not fazed by the glare from its noble eyes."},
  {"Fire Pig", 5, 99, "It loves to eat roasted berries, but sometimes it gets too excited and burns them to a crisp. It blows fire through its nose."},
  {"Fire Pig", 10, 555, "The more it eats, the more fuel it has to make the fire in its stomach stronger. When it is angered, the intensity of the flame increases."},
  {"Fire Pig", 16, 1500, "It is adept at using many different moves. It can throw a fire punch by setting its fists on fire with its fiery chin. It cares deeply about its friends."},
  {"Sea Otter", 5, 59, "The scalchop on its stomach isn't just used for battle, it can be used to break open hard berries as well. It is made from the same element as its claws."},
  {"Discipline", 8, 245, "Strict training and disclipine leads it to master its flowing double-scalchop technique. Scalchop techniques differ from one Dewott to another."},
  {"Formidable", 15, 946, "One swing of the seamitars attached to its armor can fell an opponent. A simple glare from one of them is enough to intimidate most enemies."},
  {"Scout", 5, 116, "Extremely cautious, they take shifts to maintain a constant watch of their nest. Using food stored in cheek pouches, they can keep watch for days."},
  {"Lookout", 11, 270, "Using luminescent matter, it makes its eyes and body glow and stuns attacking opponents. Keen eyesight lets them see in the dark."},
  {"Puppy", 4, 41, "It faces strong opponents with great courage. Because it doesn't yelp, it's extremely popular with Trainers who live in apartment buildings."},
  {"Loyal Dog", 9, 147, "Its dense black fur grows continuously. The high cost of keeping its hard fur properly groomed makes this a troublesome Pokemon to train."},
  {"Big-Hearted", 12, 610, "Intelligent, good-natured, and valiant, there could be no concern that it would ever attack people. Some parents even trust it to babysit."},
  {"Devious", 4, 101, "Their deceptively cute act is the perfect ruse. They steal from people for fun, but their victims can't help but forgive them."},
  {"Cruel", 11, 375, "Many Trainers are drawn to their beautiful form and fur. These Pokemon vanish and appear unexpectedly. They run silently in the night."},
  {"Grass Monkey", 6, 105, "This Pokemon dwells deep in the forest. It's good at finding berries and gathers them from all over. It's kind enough to share them with friends."},
  {"Thorn Monkey", 11, 305, "Ill tempered, it attacks enemies by swinging its barbed tail around wildly. The leaf growing on its head is very bitter."},
  {"High Temp", 6, 110, "The fire within the tuft on its head can reach up to 600oF. Very intelligent, it roasts berries before eating them. It likes to help people."},
  {"Ember", 10, 280, "It loves sweets because they become energy for the fire burning inside its body. It scatters embers from its head and tail to sear its opponents."},
  {"Spray", 6, 135, "The water stored inside the tuft of its head is rich in nutrients. It waters plants using its tail, plants that receive its water grow large."},
  {"Geyser", 10, 290, "It can shoot highly-pressurised water from its tail with enough power to break through a solid concrete wall. It prefers places with clean water."},
  {"Dream Eater", 6, 233, "This Pokemon appears before people and Pokemon who are having nightmares and eats those dreams. Munna always float in the air."},
  {"Drowsing", 11, 605, "The mist emanating from their foreheads is packed with the dreams of people and Pokemon. It changes into different colors depending on the dream that was eaten."},
  {"Tiny Pigeon", 3, 21, "This very forgetful Pokemon will wait for a new order from its Trainer even though it already has one. Flocks often gather in parks and plazas."},
  {"Wild Pigeon", 6, 150, "No matter where in the world it goes, it knows where its nest is, so it can always return to its Trainer's location regardless of the distance."},
  {"Proud", 12, 290, "Males have plumage on their heads. The females' flying abilities surpass those of the males. They will only let themselves feel close to their Trainers."},
  {"Electrified", 8, 298, "Its mane shines when it discharges electricity. They use the frequency and rhythm of these flashes to communicate with one another."},
  {"Thunderbolt", 16, 795, "When Zebstrika run at full speed, the sound of thunder reverberates. It is dangerous when it's angry as it shoots lightning from its mane in all directions."},
  {"Mantle", 4, 180, "The hexagonal cavity is its ear. It walks in the direction of sounds it hears, but if the sounds cease, it panics and topples over."},
  {"Ore", 9, 1020, "Its orange crystal is a mass of energy. Just one crystal fragment would provide enough fuel for a hundred dump trucks. When it is healthy, its core sticks out."},
  {"Compressed", 17, 2600, "The blasts of energy it makes from sunbeams have terrifying power. However, it's not able to fire its blasts at night or on rainy days."},
  {"Bat", 4, 21, "Its habitat is dark forests and caves. Suction from its nostrils enables it to stick to cave walls during sleep. It leaves a heart-shaped mark behind."},
  {"Courting", 9, 105, "Anyone who comes into contact with the ultrasonic waves emitted by a courting male experiences a positive mood shift."},
  {"Mole", 3, 85, "It can dig through the ground at a speed of 30 mph by spinning its body. It could give a car running aboveground a good race."},
  {"Subterrene", 7, 404, "More than 300 feet below the surface, they build mazelike nests. Their activity can be destructive to subway tunnels, but it can also help with construction."},
  {"Hearing", 11, 310, "Its auditory sense is astounding. Using the feelers on its ears, it can tell how someone is feeling or when an egg might hatch."},
  {"Muscular", 6, 125, "These Pokemon appear at building sites and help out with construction. They always carry squared logs. As they grow, they carry bigger logs."},
  {"Muscular", 12, 400, "They strengthen their bodies by carrying steel beams. This Pokemon is so muscular and strongly built that even a group of wrestlers could not make it budge an inch."},
  {"Muscular", 14, 870, "They use concrete pillars as walking canes. Rather than rely solely on force, they master moves that utilize the centrifugal force of spinning concrete."},
  {"Tadpole", 5, 45, "By vibrating its cheeks, it emits sound waves imperceptible to humans. It uses the rhythm of these sounds to talk and warns others of danger."},
  {"Vibration", 8, 170, "It lives in the water and on land. When they vibrate the bumps on their heads, they can make waves in water or earthquake-like vibrations on land."},
  {"Vibration", 15, 620, "It increases the power of its punches by vibrating the bumps on its fists. They can also shoot paralyzing liquid from their head bumps."},
  {"Judo", 13, 555, "When it tightens its belt, it becomes stronger. Wild Throh use vines to weave their own belts. It changes belts as it gets more powerful."},
  {"Karate", 14, 510, "The sound of Sawk punching boulders and trees can be heard all the way from the mountains where they train. Disturbing their training angers them."},
  {"Sewing", 3, 25, "It chews up leaves and sews them with sticky thread extruded from its mouth. Since this Pokemon makes its own clothes, it is a mascot for fashion designers."},
  {"Leaf-Wrapped", 5, 73, "Forests where Swadloon live have superb foliage because the nutrients they make from fallen leaves nourish the plant life."},
  {"Nurturing", 12, 205, "It keeps its eggs warm with heat from fermenting leaves. It also uses leaves to weave warm wrappings for Sewaddle by using the silk secreted from its mouth."},
  {"Centipede", 4, 53, "Using the feelers on its head and tail, it picks up vibrations in the air to determine its prey's location and state. It is brutally aggressive."},
  {"Curlipede", 12, 585, "Storing energy for evolution, it sits. But when attacked, it spins its body at high speed like a wheel and then crashes furiously into its opponent."},
  {"Megapede", 25, 2005, "With quick movements, it chases down its foes, attacking relentlessly with its horns until it prevails. Then it finishes them off with deadly poison."},
  {"Cotton Puff", 3, 6, "When it finds others of its kind, they all stick together. When enough of them have collected, the mass resembles a cumulonimbus cloud."},
  {"Windveiled", 7, 66, "It rides on the wind and slips into people's homes. After it has turned a room into a cotton-filled mess, it giggles to itself and takes off."},
  {"Bulb", 5, 66, "By pruning the leaves on its head with regularity, this Pokemon can be grown into a fine plump shape. These bitter leaves refresh those who eat them."},
  {"Flowering", 11, 163, "Even veteran Trainers face a challenge in getting its beautiful flower to bloom. It withers away if a trainer does not take good care of it."},
  {"Hostile", 10, 180, "It used to be a common food source. The meat of red Basculin is on the fatty side and it's more popular with the youth. Its temperament is vicious and aggressive."},
  {"Desert Croc", 7, 152, "It conceals itself in the sand and chomps down on the legs of any prey that unwarily walk over it. Its favorite food is Trapinch."},
  {"Desert Croc", 10, 334, "They move in groups of a few individuals. Thanks to the special membrane covering its eyes, it can see its surroundings clearly, even in the dead of night."},
  {"Intimidate", 15, 963, "Very violent Pokemon, they never allow their prey to escape. Their jaws are so powerful, they can crush the body of an automobile."},
  {"Zen Charm", 6, 375, "When its internal fire is burning, it cannot calm down and it runs around. When the fire diminishes, it pulls its limbs into its body and falls asleep."},
  {"Blazing", 13, 929, "When one is injured in a fierce battle, it transforms into a stone statue. Then it meditates and sharpens its mind and fights on mentally."},
  {"Cactus", 10, 280, "Arid regions are their habitat. When it moves rhythmically, it makes a sound similar to maracas, making the surprised Pokemon flee."},
  {"Rock Inn", 3, 145, "It makes a hole in a stone of a suitable size. If that rock breaks, the Pokemon remains agitated until it locates a replacement."},
  {"Stone Home", 14, 2000, "Competing for territory, Crustle fight viciously. The one whose boulder is broken is the loser of the battle and begins to weaken."},
  {"Shedding", 6, 118, "Its skin has a rubbery elasticity, so it can reduce damage by defensively pulling its skin up to its neck. Its skull is massively thick."},
  {"Hoodlum", 11, 300, "Groups of them beat up anything that enters their territory. The one with the biggest crest is the group leader, and is the most respected."},
  {"Avianoid", 14, 140, "The guardians of an ancient city, they always fly the same route while keeping watch for invaders. They use their psychic power to attack enemies."},
  {"Spirit", 5, 15, "These Pokemon arose from the spirits of people interred in graves in past ages. Each of them carries a mask that used to be its face when it was human."},
  {"Coffin", 17, 765, "Grave robbers who mistake them for real coffins and get too close end up trapped inside their bodies. Their bodies are covered in pure gold."},
  {"Prototurtle", 7, 165, "Reputed to be the ancestor of most turtle Pokemon, it lived in warm seas about a hundred million years ago. It was restored from a fossil."},
  {"Prototurtle", 12, 810, "They can live both in the ocean and on land. Incredible jaw strength enables them to chew up steel beams and rocks along with their prey."},
  {"First Bird", 5, 95, "Said to be the ancestor of all bird Pokemon, Archen itself could not actually fly but moved by hopping from treetop to treetop."},
  {"First Bird", 14, 320, "They are intelligent and will cooperate to catch prey. When one Archeops had the prey cornered, another would swoop on it."},
  {"Trash Bag", 6, 310, "It gorges on trash until its stomach is full. Then it belches toxic gas. An unlucky whiff of this gas will put a person in the hospital."},
  {"Trash Heap", 19, 1073, "Beware the poisonous liquid it shoots from its right arm. If even a little of it gets on you, you'll experience the full effects of this unidentified toxin."},
  {"Tricky Fox", 7, 125, "To protect themselves from danger, they hide their true identities by transforming into people and Pokemon. Apparently, it often transforms into a silent child."},
  {"Illusion Fox", 16, 811, "Bonds between these Pokemon are very strong. It protects the safety of its pack by tricking its opponents. They defend their lair with illusory scenery."},
  {"Chinchilla", 4, 58, "These Pokemon prefer a tidy habitat. They greet one another by rubbing each other with their tails, which are always kept well groomed and clean."},
  {"Scarf", 5, 75, "Their white fur feels amazing to touch. Cinccino's body is coated in a special oil that repels dust and helps it deflect attacks, such as punches."},
  {"Fixation", 4, 58, "They intently observe both Trainers and Pokemon. Apparently, Gothita are looking at something that only they can see. Their ribbonlike feelers increase their power."},
  {"Manipulate", 7, 180, "Starlight is the source of their power. They use hypnosis to control people and Pokemon. Tales of Gothorita leading them astray are told in every corner."},
  {"Astral Body", 15, 440, "Starry skies thousands of light-years away are visible in the space distorted by their intense psychic power. When it learns its Trainer's life span, it cries in sadness."},
  {"Cell", 3, 10, "Because their bodies are enveloped in a special liquid, they are fine in any environment, no matter how severe. They can use telepathy to talk with others."},
  {"Mitosis", 6, 80, "When their brains, now divided in two, are thinking the same thoughts, these Pokemon exhibit their maximized psychic power."},
  {"Multiplying", 10, 201, "They use psychic power to control their arms, which are made of a special liquid. When Reuniclus shake hands, a network forms between their brains."},
  {"Water Bird", 5, 55, "These bird Pokemon are excellent divers. They are better at swimming than flying, and they happily eat their favorite food, peat moss, as they dive underwater."},
  {"White Bird", 13, 242, "Despite their elegant appearance, they can flap their wings strongly and fly for thousands of miles. The one in the middle is the leader of the flock."},
  {"Fresh Snow", 4, 57, "The temperature of their breath is -58oF. They create snow crystals and make snow fall in the areas around them. Vanillite is treasured by households in warm regions."},
  {"Icy Snow", 11, 410, "Vanillish has existed since the Ice Age. It controls particles of ice, freezes its opponents, and then shatters them with a headbutt."},
  {"Snowstorm", 13, 575, "Each of its two heads has a brain, and when they are in agreement, it attacks its enemies by exhaling a violent blizzard. It makes snow clouds inside its body."},
  {"Season", 6, 195, "Deerling have different scents depending on the season. In early spring, these Pokemon give off a delicate, sweet, and calming scent."},
  {"Season", 19, 925, "Some people call Sawsbuck the harbingers of spring because the plants growing on its horns change according to the season. The leader possesses magnificent horns."},
  {"Sky Squirrel", 4, 50, "It glides using its cape-like membrane. It grills berries and bug Pokemon with electric shocks from the pouches on its cheeks and makes a meal of them."},
  {"Clamping", 5, 59, "When they feel threatened, they spit an acidic liquid to drive attackers away. For some reason they evolve while they are in the same place as Shelmet."},
  {"Cavalry", 10, 330, "Wearing the shell covering they stole from Shelmet, they defend themselves and attack with two lances. The steel armor protects their whole body."},
  {"Mushroom", 2, 10, "It lures Pokemon in with its pattern that looks just like a Poke Ball, then releases its poison spores. Why it resembles a Poke Ball is unknown."},
  {"Mushroom", 6, 105, "It lures prey close by dancing and waving its arm caps, which resemble Poke Balls, in a swaying motion, but very few Pokemon are fooled by this."},
  {"Floating", 12, 330, "If its veil-like arms stun and wrap an opponent, that foe will be dragged five miles below the surface to its lair, never to return."},
  {"Floating", 22, 1350, "They propel themselves by expelling absorbed seawater from their bodies. It's said there's a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor."},
  {"Caring", 12, 316, "When they find a wounded Pokemon, they embrace it and bring it to shore. The special membrane enveloping Alomomola has the ability to heal wounds."},
  {"Attaching", 1, 6, "Since they can't generate their own electricity, they attach themselves to large-bodied Pokemon and absorb static electricity, which they store in a pouch."},
  {"EleSpider", 8, 143, "It creates barriers from electrified silk that stun foes. This works as a weapon as well as a defense. While it is immobilized by shock, they leisurely consume it."},
  {"Thorn Seed", 6, 188, "It absorbs the iron it finds in the rock while clinging to the ceiling of caves. When threatened, it attacks by shooting a barrage of spikes."},
  {"Thorn Pod", 10, 1100, "It fights by swinging around its three spiky feelers and shooting spikes. A hit from these steel spikes can reduce a boulder to rubble."},
  {"Gear", 3, 210, "Two bodies comprise a fixed pair. The two minigears that mesh together are predetermined. Each will rebound from other minigears without meshing."},
  {"Gear", 6, 510, "A minigear and big gear comprise its body. Spinning minigears are rotated at high speed and repeatedly fired away. It is dangerous if the gears don't return."},
  {"Gear", 6, 810, "Its red core functions as an energy tank. It is rotated at high speed for a rapid energy charge. It fires the charged energy through its spikes into an area."},
  {"EleFish", 2, 3, "These Pokemon move in schools. One alone can emit only a trickle of electricity, so a group of them gathers to unleash a powerful electric shock."},
  {"EleFish", 12, 220, "These Pokemon have a big appetite. It wraps itself around its prey and paralyzes it with electricity from the round spots on its sides. Then it chomps."},
  {"EleFish", 21, 805, "They crawl out of the ocean using their arms. They will attack prey on shore and immediately drag it into the ocean, with their sucker mouths."},
  {"Cerebral", 5, 90, "It psychically squeezes the brain of its foe, causing unendurable headaches. Rumors of its origin are linked to a UFO crash site in the desert 50 years ago."},
  {"Cerebral", 10, 345, "It can manipulate an opponent's memory. Apparently, it communicates by flashing its three fingers, but those patterns haven't been decoded."},
  {"Candle", 3, 31, "While Litwick shines a light and pretends to be a guide, it absorbs the life force of any who follow it, which becomes the fuel that it burns."},
  {"Lamp", 6, 130, "This ominous Pokemon is feared. Through cities it wanders, searching for the spirits of the fallen. The spirits it absorbs fuel its baleful fire."},
  {"Luring", 10, 343, "Being consumed in Chandelure's flame burns up the spirit, leaving the body behind. By waving the flames on its arms, it puts its foes into a hypnotic trance."},
  {"Tusk", 6, 180, "They mark their territory by leaving gashes in trees with their tusks. If a tusk breaks, a new one grows in quickly, harder and sturdier than the last."},
  {"Axe Jaw", 10, 360, "Their tusks can shatter rocks. A broken tusk will not grow back, so it diligently sharpens its tusks on river rocks after the end of a battle."},
  {"Axe Jaw", 18, 1055, "They are kind but can be relentless when defending territory. Their sturdy tusks will stay sharp even if used to cut steel beams."},
  {"Chill", 5, 85, "Its nose is always running. Their snot is a barometer of health. When healthy, their snot is sticky and the power of their ice moves increases."},
  {"Freezing", 26, 2600, "It freezes its breath to create fangs and claws of ice to fight with. Very able in the water, it swims around in northern seas and catches prey."},
  {"Crystallize", 11, 1480, "They are born in snow clouds. When its body temperature goes up, it turns into steam and vanishes. When its temperature lowers, it returns to ice."},
  {"Snail", 4, 77, "When attacked, it defends itself by closing the lid of its shell. It evolves when bathed in an electric-like energy along with Karrablast."},
  {"Shell Out", 8, 253, "When its body dries out, it weakens. So, to prevent dehydration, it wraps itself in layers of thin membrane. It is very light and fights with ninja-like movements."},
  {"Trap", 7, 110, "It conceals itself in the mud of the seashore. Then it waits. When prey touch it, it delivers a jolt of electricity. It smiles when transmitting electricity."},
  {"Martial Arts", 9, 200, "They have mastered elegant combos. As they concentrate, their battle moves become swifter and more precise. What it lacks in power, it makes up for in quantity."},
  {"Martial Arts", 14, 355, "They use the long fur on their arms as a whip to strike their opponents. Its arm attacks come with such rapidity that they cannot even be seen."},
  {"Cave", 16, 1390, "It warms its body by absorbing sunlight with its wings. When its body temperature falls, it can no longer move. It uses its sharp claws to catch prey."},
  {"Automaton", 10, 920, "These Pokemon are thought to have been created by the science of an ancient and mysterious civilization. It's been active for thousands of years."},
